      },
      "body": "### Description\r\nFixes #9364.\r\n\r\nWhen sending an empty form value (`\"\"`) for sequence bytes annotations (e.g. `list[bytes]` or `Annotated[list[bytes], File()]`) from Swagger UI or other clients, `_extract_form_body` in `fastapi/dependencies/utils.py` unconditionally called `await sub_value.read()`. Because `sub_value` is an empty string `\"\"` rather than an `UploadFile`, an `AttributeError: 'str' object has no attribute 'read'` was raised.\r\n\r\n### Solution\r\nAs discussed in #9364 and incorporating feedback from @Jeanlaris:\r\n- Guard `sub_value` inside the `is_bytes_sequence_annotation` loop to check `if isinstance(sub_value, UploadFile) or hasattr(sub_value, \"read\"):` before awaiting `.read()`.\r\n- Primitive string values fall back cleanly to `results.append(sub_value)`, matching the existing type annotation `results: list[bytes | str] = []` and allowing Pydantic to handle downstream validation cleanly.\r\n\r\n### Tests\r\n- Added unit regression tests in `tests/test_optional_file_list.py` covering:\r\n  - Optional bytes list with empty form value (`data={\"files\": \"\"}`).\r\n  - Annotated bytes list with empty form value.\r\n  - Required bytes list with empty form value.\r\n- All 10 file/form tests and full test suites pass.",
      "changed_files": 2,
      "closed_at": null,
      "comments": 0,
      "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16357/comments",
      "commits": 2,
